{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective","id":850777,"title":"Necromancers from Wraith perspective","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-21T13:31:26-07:00","id":850777,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Necromancers from Wraith perspective","content":"So I have a question here, from a Vampire player to Wraith players.<br /> How do Restless Dead react to Necromancers(such as Giovanni Vampires)?<br /> Is their existence common knowledge or are the wraiths who become slaves to necromancers are unfortunate few?<br /> How Wraith populate places with proximity to necromancers? Do they warn each other that the threat exists, or do they avoid places like that all together?<br /> Do Wraith Institutions such as Hiearachy have some countermeasures or policy towards them? Do they avoid provoking them to keep larger Wraith society a secret or do they organize in groups to find a way to fight back?<br /> What happens if group of Wraiths finds out their friend started running spy-errands for some pale dude all of a sudden. What will they do to help him, and will they do anything at all.<br /> <br /> In Vampire Lore, Giovanni kidnap Wraiths in huge numbers, and over the course of history they came close to a million souls held captive.<br /> Is this noticed by a larger Wraith community and does it have any reflection what so ever in Wraith books?<br /> <br /> Also, it would be helpful if someone gave me a crash-course on what useful Arcanoi Wraith can use to benefit(or hurt) the Vampire Necromancer.<br /> <br /> UPD: These forums are pretty dead, aint they?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","user":"LordOfCinder","date":". 03-23-2016, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T11:36:04-07:00","id":851895,"title":"","content":"The wraiths are aware. They hate the Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:22:24-07:00","id":852324,"title":"","content":"That's really helpful,dude. Real detailed. Tons of insight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:32:16-07:00","id":852330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=852324#post852324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really helpful,dude. Real detailed. Tons of insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about you read a book or search the white wolf wiki?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T06:40:24-07:00","id":852377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=852330#post852330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about you read a book or search the white wolf wiki?</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think I didn't do that? Vampires are not exactly the most important thing in Wraith. <br /> How much White Wolf wiki will help a Wraith player to get his head around what Vampires can do or cant? Or how Vampire society may or may not react to one thing or the other. Which Disciplines can target ghosts and which can't?<br /> Every World of Darkness setting has its own know-hows and logic which comes with experience.<br /> <br /> I came to these sub-forum to exchange information and cool ideas, and what I get is this. I don't really understand the reason for that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T08:00:06-07:00","id":852435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=852377#post852377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes you think I didn't do that? Vampires are not exactly the most important thing in Wraith. <br /> How much White Wolf wiki will help a Wraith player to get his head around what Vampires can do or cant? Or how Vampire society may or may not react to one thing or the other. Which Disciplines can target ghosts and which can't?<br /> Every World of Darkness setting has its own know-hows and logic which comes with experience.<br /> <br /> I came to these sub-forum to exchange information and cool ideas, and what I get is this. I don't really understand the reason for that.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Read Clanbook: Giovanni? Read Mediums: Speakers with the Dead? Those have the info you require. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, trying to summarise the entirety of wraiths' interactions with necromancers would take too long and I'm not required to provide you with detail. You asked a question and I answered it. I've now gone on to explain where you can go to find some further information.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, the answer is kinda up to you and the demands of your game. It's not hard to extrapolate how wraiths would react to necromancers, but this is something best played out. The needs of your game may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T08:42:42-07:00","id":852442,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective#post850777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">UPD: These forums are pretty dead, aint they?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> Hey-Ooooh!<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll try to fill in some of the blanks with musings based (more or less) on canon. Keep in mind that WtO Second Edition had perspectives based on an older version of the game. For example, the two big (only?) Necromancy vampires were the Samedi and Giovanni (and Nagarja, which I want to call Naranja \u2013 which is hilarious without the proper amount of caffeine!).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective#post850777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do Restless Dead react to Necromancers (such as Giovanni Vampires)?<br /> Is their existence common knowledge or are the wraiths who become slaves to necromancers are unfortunate few?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> In WtO Second, three Clans are listed as antagonists; the Giovanni and the Tremere. The Samedi were also mentioned, but with less hostility (iirc). This was also when Necromancy was built like a normal Discipline, without Paths and Rituals.<br /> To be honest, \u201cThe wraiths are aware. They hate the Giovanni,\u201d is fairly accurate. Between wards and bindings, however, many of the wraithly enslaved have few \u2013 if any options \u2013 of retribution.<br /> There\u2019s also a funny power dichotomy. Older wraiths \u2013 some have been around as long as some vampire \u2013 have the supernatural wherewithal to resist Necromancy and go toe-to-toe with ectoplasmic Slavers. Older wraiths tend to lose touch with their Fetters [things that anchor them to the world of the living] and spend almost all their time in the Tempest [the deep underworld proper, away from the lands of the living]. The likelihood of a Giovanni summoning and binding one of these ghostly badasses is very slim.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective#post850777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How Wraith populate places with proximity to necromancers? Do they warn each other that the threat exists, or do they avoid places like that all together?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> Wraiths like to hang out in places called Haunts. Haunts are buildings that have a lot of death mojo. These places tend to have a lighter Shroud (think ghost Gauntlet) which makes some of their powers easier. I think it also makes some Necromancy powers easier as well, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective#post850777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do Wraith Institutions such as Hierarchy have some countermeasures or policy towards them? Do they avoid provoking them to keep larger Wraith society a secret or do they organize in groups to find a way to fight back?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> Stygian society [the oppressive government of the \u201cWestern\u201d dead] enforces a law called Dictum Mortuum (sp?). It\u2019s a catchall stipulation against interfering with the lands of the living. Depending on the legal interpretation (both IC and OOC), it could (or couldn\u2019t) apply to vampires. Some groups in the Hierarchy (such as the Grim Legion) will turn a blind-eye to wraiths avenging their own murders, even if that murder took place at the fangs of a vampire.<br /> <br /> In the halls of Stygian power, there are several Legions based on how people died. Each Legion is led by a Deathlord. These are ghosts that are somewhere between vampire elder and methuselah (-ish). Below them are less powerful but no-less-impressive ghosts. They exist exclusively in the deep underworld (the Tempest, where Stygia proper is located). They don\u2019t have much, if any, interaction with the vampires.<br /> <br /> I imagine Deathlords react to vampires summoning their Legionaries in the same way corporate CEOs react to their employees getting called for jury duty; it\u2019s a pain in the ass but as long as someone else fills his spot and his work gets done, they don\u2019t really care.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t touch on Enoch\u2026<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective#post850777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, it would be helpful if someone gave me a crash-course on what useful Arcanoi Wraith can use to benefit (or hurt) the Vampire Necromancer.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> Off the top of my head, in no particular order:<br /> <br /> Pandemonium: Poltergeist/Beetlejuice-type stuff.<br /> Outrage: GhostPunchitude<br /> Puppetry: Skinriding and possession. I\u2019m not sure about vampires, but maybe ghouls?<br /> Embody: Manifesting a wraith\u2019s Corpus [ectoplasmic body] across the Shroud and into the real world.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 03-24-2016, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T08:48:50-07:00","id":852444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=852435#post852435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...this is something best played out. The needs of your game may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Also, this!<br /> If you want wraiths and vampires to have a more symbiotic relationship (like goblins and wizards in the Harry Potter universe?), go for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:24:05-07:00","id":852598,"title":"","content":"I remember the last time I had some vamps cross wraiths, some wraith had an Arcanos that let him light things on fire. That was VERY effective at getting the vamps to leave post--haste. I can't remember which Arcanos it was off the top of my head. Outrage? Pandemonium?<br /> <br /> Wraiths have a LOT of powers, so their ability to mess with vampires they don't like is limited only by creative application (and possible arrest for violation of the Dictum in some necropoli). They could dissolve the wall of a haven and let the sunshine in with Alchemy. Or break it down with Outrage. If you think vamps dream while down for the count, they can make their daytime &quot;rest&quot; a living hell. Between Puppetry and Inhabit (depending on how you slice the animation factor of a vampire's body), it's pretty easy to walk through the walls of a vamps haven while he's asleep, possess him and have him go sunbathing.<br /> <br /> I'm sure most necromancers use Ward Against Ghosts to protect themselves from angry ghosts. There are a lot more wraiths in your average necropolis than vampires in the Skinlands version of the same. Pissing off a lot of them by flagrant use of Necromancy is probably not wise. I'm betting the Giovanni as just as much &quot;rats in the walls&quot; of the Shadowlands as they are in the vampire world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 03-25-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:40:35-07:00","id":854120,"title":"","content":"Thank you fellas, that was really helpful.<br /> <br /> Nazfool's post was just what I was looking for. Brief and detailed at the same time=)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T19:10:39-07:00","id":854314,"title":"","content":"I believe Wraith: the Great War mentions an organization called the Bloody Legion, formed by members of the Grim Legion (the ghost of those that died by violence) that combat necromancers who try to enslave wraiths.<br /> <br /> Vampire has a tendency to make it seem like vampires are on top, and therefore portray the Giovanni as just dominating wraiths. My own view is that this is grossly exaggerated. I believe that Giovanni likely only enslave those wraiths their own mortal family produces, plus any associates. Its very limited in terms of wraiths of completely unassociated with the Giovanni - say those wraiths that interfere with them. I believe the whole million wraiths enslaved just is not possible from the perspective of the Wraith game - certainly not in the time frame when the Giovanni have been operational. Then again, I also see the Giovanni clan as being much smaller in number than other people.<br /> <br /> The Hierarchy actually has a lot resources at its disposal, and it can make things very difficult for their enemies.<br /> <br /> I believe there are a lot of red lines in place, and provided the Giovanni limit their depridations and don't cause trouble for wraiths protected by the Hierarchy, they are left alone. In turn, the Giovanni don't bother wraiths outside their purview.<br /> <br /> The fact is if you review the enemies of the Hierarchy, necromancers like the Giovanni are really low on the totem pole in terms of risk and danger. The Hierarchy could squash them like a bug, but need to concentrate on bigger threats. This doesn't mean the Giovanni can do whatever they like, but there are limits. As long as Giovanni stay with them, the Hierarchy ignores them or limits their responses. If the Giovanni get too big for their britches, then the big dogs come out.<br /> <br /> But it all depends on the assumptions you make in your own games, and what you need in terms of plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T03:55:04-07:00","id":854407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854314#post854314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact is if you review the enemies of the Hierarchy, necromancers like the Giovanni are really low on the totem pole in terms of risk and danger. The Hierarchy could squash them like a bug, but need to concentrate on bigger threats. This doesn't mean the Giovanni can do whatever they like, but there are limits. As long as Giovanni stay with them, the Hierarchy ignores them or limits their responses. If the Giovanni get too big for their britches, then the big dogs come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That what I always had hard time getting my head around. On the one hand Vampire Necromancers are not nearly as numerous as Wraith's. Necromancy however has some hardcore effects, and it's strange that in official books there are no reaction to that. I mean Necromancers can bind ghosts and send them across the world, collect 5 to 6 of them in a &quot;magic jar&quot;(!) or make them violate there own laws(force them to interact with skinlands).<br /> It is also a big mystery why Necromancers themselves apparently know NOTHING about larger Underworld(or know little).<br /> I would like to portray Underworld as full of potential retaliation in my game, but logic of the setting really confuses me sometimes. I am strictly against X can squash Y like a bug in World of Darkness though. It doesn't make a good story, IMO.<br /> <br /> So far my idea is that during the game, Necro players will witness ghostly legion entering the city and maybe their interactions with ghosts will become less safe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854314#post854314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hierarchy actually has a lot resources at its disposal, and it can make things very difficult for their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>What resources except for raw manpower and relic suicide bombers?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","user":"LordOfCinder","date":". 03-28-2016, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:14:57-07:00","id":854533,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854407#post854407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is also a big mystery why Necromancers themselves apparently know NOTHING about larger Underworld(or know little).</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> I see it is a matter of not caring and/or not thinking to ask. They have this ectoplasmic peon, they know ghosts are real, etc., but probably don\u2019t think to ask about the larger underworld.<br /> <br /> Also, the wraiths that vampiric necromancers are summoning might not be the most knowledgeable when it comes to the Tempest and what not. OOC, wraith players are confused by the layout the underworld sometimes (I\u2019ll admit to it). If players \u2013 with access to gaming books - get confused, imagine how confusing it must be for a freshly dead wraith. <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854407#post854407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So far my idea is that during the game, Necro players will witness ghostly legion entering the city and maybe their interactions with ghosts will become less safe.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> I dig it. Maybe it\u2019s a quiet town (on one side of the Shroud) with a few dozen wraiths that are fodder for the necromancers. One of their \u201ccontacts\u201d gives them a warning; something called the Hierarchy is coming into the city.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854407#post854407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What resources except for raw manpower and relic suicide bombers?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> Please keep in mind, some of this depends on how you run things with WtO and pending changes from Wr20. Some of this is from my table and other bits are from the books.<br /> <br /> I think my favorite \u201ckill a fangbanger\u201d tactic used at my table is the use of Embody by someone proficiently wielding a Stygian Steel sword. It\u2019s a sword made out souls, tempered with ore mined from hell\u2026basically. Since Stygian steel weapons inflict aggravated damage to wraiths my troupe inferred that they cause aggravated damage to any hapless supernatural critter unlucky enough to be caught by its edge. We also inferred that Embody allows wraiths to bring in-possession relics/artifacts across the Shroud with them (completely unlike the process becoming Risen).<br /> <br /> Imagine a Hierarchy-sanctioned strike force (given leave to break the Dictum Mortuum and cross the Shroud via Embody) and armed with weapons that can send a vampire to Final Death, deployed to deal with a \u201ctroublesome\u201d necromancer.<br /> <br /> The other example, on the extreme other end of the spectrum is Enoch. Specifically, what happened to Enoch. In the fiction between chapters in <i>Book of the Legions</i>, when asked if he possesses a nuke the Smiling Lord (one of the uber-wraith Deathlords) responds with, \u201cOne, several, let\u2019s not quibble over numbers.\u201d If push came to shove and Stygia decided that a group of vampires needed to be ash, they could make it happen. Clan Giovanni, for all their \u201clord of the dead\u201d talk, doesn\u2019t interfere with Stygian business that much. As far as the Deathlords are concerned, even Uncle Augie is just an occasional nuisance.<br /> <br /> The best way to think about the capabilities of the Hierarchy is to imagine the military capabilities of a modern country (the largest I think are the PRC and USA) and make some small tweaks. Bullets, for example, are harder to come by but every soldier has some supernatural ability. Then make the leaders of that country on-par with vampire methuselahs.<br /> <br /> I imagine it\u2019s not just capabilities; the cost is equally horrific. The Pathos (ghostly version of Blood Points) needed to power the equipment, the time it takes to call in reserve Legionaries, the logistics of leaving Necropoli (centers of wraithly population) poorly defended, etc. This sort of thing would be astronomically expensive. A small coterie of blood-drinking necromancers that summon and bind Shadowland-bound wraiths may not be worth the time it takes to organize a strike force. Unless, of course, the coteries has done something majorly piss off an Anacreon (kind of like a Prince-ish).<br /> <br /> [Note: I\u2019m sure there are a few things I\u2019m forgetting or haven\u2019t considered but other forum users will bring them up.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ]<br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:17:21-07:00","id":854535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854407#post854407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What resources except for raw manpower and relic suicide bombers?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably something akin to the Doomslayers. A contingent of gaunt bio-exorcists sanctioned that highest levels who have permission to use all sorts of Arcanoi that are typically forbidden by the Dictum. There are A LOT of ways vampires could be made utterly miserable (to the point of True Death) by such and few of them take relic suicide bombers or raw manpower (more specific application of expertise and a lot of it). <br /> <br /> A single Necromancer causing medial levels of disturbance to the functioning of the necropolis would be the Anacreon's problem and the solution would need to be appropriately discrete, but anyone causing significant disturbances would probably be able to ask for help from Stygia (Oh, the loss of face!) and get 1 or so of these bad boys out to handle their problems. A full-on action would probably take a rapacious cabal of Necromancers without any care or subtlety.<br /> <br /> There are a LOT more wraiths than vampires, so the numbers would end up being in the Hierarchy's favor if they wished to bring the force of the Dark Kingdom against offending vampires. <br /> <br /> But, the Hierarchy probably doesn't care so much about unaffiliated wraiths, Renegades or Heretics, so it would be possible to target such wraiths (Membership does have it's privileges). And it would be possible to simply &quot;luck out&quot; and end up snagging such wraiths as the vast majority of those the Necromancer is necromancing. <br /> <br /> Oh, plus, I'm sure, there are wraiths out there that are more than happy to add Necromancers to their client list. Look at the economy of Stygia. Selling off other wraiths to Necromancers would just be another market, possibly a chancey one if the Dictum applies, but, oh, the FAVORS that could be exchanged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T12:28:05-07:00","id":854595,"title":"","content":"My suspicion is that the 'million wraiths' thing refers to *every wraith the Giovanni have every caught*, rather than all those currently in captivity. Otherwise it's simply a lie (remember how the Crazy 88 didn't really have 88 members?). Then again, there are potentially billions of wraiths in the Underworld, so maybe they do. Maybe they're all drones animated by the will of the necromancer who summons them? That would make more sense.<br /> <br /> I've also always played the Giovanni as a tiny clan, in comparison to the others. They aren't numerous enough to cause most necropoli any real trouble. And those wraiths they do enslave are presumably unable to become spectres or, if they can, are unable to cause havoc because they're bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-31-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:49:51-07:00","id":855098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854595#post854595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suspicion is that the 'million wraiths' thing refers to *every wraith the Giovanni have every caught*, rather than all those currently in captivity. Otherwise it's simply a lie (remember how the Crazy 88 didn't really have 88 members?). Then again, there are potentially billions of wraiths in the Underworld, so maybe they do. Maybe they're all drones animated by the will of the necromancer who summons them? That would make more sense.<br /> <br /> I've also always played the Giovanni as a tiny clan, in comparison to the others. They aren't numerous enough to cause most necropoli busy. And those wraiths they do enslave are presumably unable to become spectres or, if they can, are unable to cause havoc because they're bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one million number is the goal. They aren't there yet, and may not be for centuries. There was a time recently when they were starting to get close, but the Week of Nightmares set a lot of their captured wraiths loose and the Giovanni have been struggling to recoup the loss.<br /> <br /> In my view of Necromancers and deeper understanding of the underworld, those veteran and well-read Necromancers who actually know about Stygia and its workings also know enough to leave it alone. It benefits them far more to poach weaker vulnerable wraiths from the more easily accessible Shadowlands than to try and dig up some unwieldy deathless monster from the depths. I also think Stygia mostly turns a blind eye to Necromancers because they provide an inducement for wayward wraiths to seek safety in Stygia away from the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> If the Giovanni were to try and launch a full scale Necromantic invasion of Stygia I think they could probably inflict a cataclysmic amount of damage, but not without significant casualties and cost to their resources, something which would leave them vulnerable to reprisal from both any Stygian remnants and from their innumerable vampiric rivals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:07:03-07:00","id":855704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854595#post854595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They aren't numerous enough to cause most necropoli busy. And those wraiths they do enslave are presumably unable to become spectres or, if they can, are unable to cause havoc because they're bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit slaves turning from spirito to spettro is actually a primary peril for necromancers. They are not entirely sure why and how that happens though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, plus, I'm sure, there are wraiths out there that are more than happy to add Necromancers to their client list. Look at the economy of Stygia. Selling off other wraiths to Necromancers would just be another market, possibly a chancey one if the Dictum applies, but, oh, the FAVORS that could be exchanged. </div> </div> </div>That is A-idea. I love it, Ajax.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:19:19-07:00","id":855706,"title":"","content":"Sleazy talent agent needs to make a living in the afterlife somehow","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T08:32:54-07:00","id":855708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=855098#post855098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Giovanni were to try and launch a full scale Necromantic invasion of Stygia I think they could probably inflict a cataclysmic amount of damage, but not without significant casualties and cost to their resources, something which would leave them vulnerable to reprisal from both any Stygian remnants and from their innumerable vampiric rivals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full scale Invasions and the like, is to epic for World of Darkness IMO. Besides its rather pointless.<br /> And yeah, I kind of agree that even knowing about Stygia changes little it terms of necromantic affairs. You cant get there anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T09:31:25-07:00","id":855741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=855708#post855708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Full scale Invasions and the like, is to epic for World of Darkness IMO. Besides its rather pointless.<br /> And yeah, I kind of agree that even knowing about Stygia changes little it terms of necromantic affairs. You cant get there anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just might just end up in a pissing match between VtM partisans vs. WtO fans, BUT, for the mental exercise...<br /> <br /> (Assuming Augustus isn't indisposed), a young Antediluvian + some elder-ish childer + the rest of the Clan +1,000,000 wraiths<br /> <br /> vs.<br /> <br /> Charon (assuming HE isn't indisposed) + the Deathlords + the gaunts of Stygia + the rest of the Hierarchy + (pretty likely) the Ferrymen + (possibly) the Lady of Fate<br /> <br /> You'd have to run some Wraith version of the Fermi Equation to figure out how many wraiths are in the Hierarchy, but it's probably likely a lot more than 1,000,000 + the non-elder Giovanni and whoever else (ghouls?) the Giovanni could bring. So numbers would edge to the the Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Power-wise, the Hierarchy is composed of wraiths who tend to have more powers per individual and by age than vamps typically get and their powers are largely much more applicable to the environment. That leaves the Giovanni fighting on Sun Tzu's &quot;dangerous ground&quot;. In addition, the logistical problems of supplying manpower and power-power from Stygia pale in comparison to the the difficulties of projecting power across the Shroud. The relative actual power of the &quot;Big Guns&quot; would probably depend on perspective. Maybe Augustus is equivalent to, say Charon, but he might be more like a younger Deathlord. (Unless he's actually just Capadocious's finger-puppet, which would change things). This is definitely the part where the pissing match comes into play.<br /> <br /> All in all, the Giovanni look seriously outclassed if their objective is to overthrow the Hierarchy. It's like having Uruguay take on Brazil or Cyprus itch to get into a fight with the EU or the Nabateans trying to take down the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> The only hope the Giovanni have to cause more than &quot;difficulties&quot; are if the can manage some asymmetric warfare, or, even better, play to their strengths and make some deals with specters and Renegades and maybe another Dark Kingdom. The Hierarchy would be much more vulnerable to a Giovanni incursion if they were dealing with Giovanni-assisted Renegade and Heretic insurgents while trying to fend off a war with the Dark Kingdom of Jade and specters boiling out of random nihils and causing all sorts of problems. Particularly if they can make some REALLY good deals... a hektonahire coming up the Veinous Stair or taking the Ferrymen out by &quot;painting&quot; with some Necromancy to make them become easier targets for their Pasiphae, or something else(perhaps, even, Enoch...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T09:43:18-07:00","id":855751,"title":"","content":"Any major incursion into the Shadowlands would end with the current crop of Deathlords having another set of ashtrays. <br /> <br /> On the timescale of WoD, the Giovanni are very, very young. Half the upper crust of Stygia (the city) is older, probably more experienced, and definitely more ruthless than their founder. The Giovanni merely deal in souls, Stygia uses them as coin.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:27:42-07:00","id":855774,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">It\u2019s fun speculating, especially as a fan of WtO, VtM, and [fantasy] Necromancy in general.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Cainite necromancers and the Hierarchy would ever have a reason for an all-out war. Even in <i>Book of Legions</i>, the \u201cwar\u201d against Enoch was painted as a handy target to be used to unite the Empire. It wasn\u2019t a threat to Stygia and the Deathlords knew it.<br /> <br /> It may be an oversimplification, but the controlling powers of the Hierarchy and the elders of [insert Clan with Necromancy] aren\u2019t even concerned with the same worlds. They might as well be Titan and Europa for all the Deathlords/elders care. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:48:27-07:00","id":855787,"title":"","content":"The first Wraith game (and only Wraith game) I ever ran was set in a small-town Necropolis in northern Louisiana. The problem was that of the few residents, some were beginning to vanish. The players had time to discover it was the work of a vampiric necromancer living in a trailer park on the edge of town before one of the players got a new job schedule and the game ended. Vamps make for fun antagonists, but you really have to tweak their stats or they just don't interact with Wraiths that much unless they have MAD dots of Necromancy and TONS of Rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:05:43-07:00","id":856221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=854407#post854407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What resources except for raw manpower and relic suicide bombers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to remember that the Hierarchy is the only supernatural organization that is large enough that they have an actual government, economy, and military forces. They just don't have large numbers, they have organization. They have specialists and other highly trained wraiths. If they have trouble in the Skinlands, they don't send some ignorant and half trained circle of wraiths who have been around a few years. They have the equivalents of special forces armed with artifacts supported by masters of Arcanoi that have trained for decades or perhaps centuries along with Barghests or legendary creatures.<br /> <br /> They are heavily organized because that's what the Hierarchy needs to be to survive Great Malestroms, hordes of spectres, and the other forces of Oblivion. Any organization that creates a system with Equitae, Doomslayers, Office of Maelstrong Preparedness, Institute for Obliviographic Studies, Magesterium Veritas, and the Online Legion as well as builds Citadels, Beacons, and Tempest Ports is an organization that is on the ball.<br /> <br /> Operating in the Skinlands is difficult, but masters of Embody, Puppetry, Outrage, Pandemonium, and other disciplines that exist solely to screw with people in the Skinlands can cause a lot of damage. A well timed use of Outrage or Inhabit can cause a car crash, or a house to burn down. A Giovanni's Allies, Contacts, or Retainers can be puppeted to eliminate them through death, scandal, or criminal activity. Determined wraiths can find out information and secrets and pass them on to enemies.<br /> <br /> In other words, it would not be hard to more or less destroy any Giovanni's influence, allies, or support, and also convince people to hunt them down and kill them.<br /> <br /> Too many times in discussions about supernatural creatures in the World of Darkness and who is &quot;tougher&quot;, people only compare direct attacks. In actuality, almost no supernatural creature is going to go one on one versus the other. They are going to strike in indirect ways that build on their strengths and their enemies' weaknesses.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that this would be easy for the Hierarchy. They are only going to mobilize such assets if the threats are worth the cost. But if the Giovanni really were as dangerous as the Clanbook &quot;propaganda&quot; makes them out to be, then the Hierarchy would do so.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Giovanni could fight back, but it is going to cost them a lot to do so which will just weaken them against their enemies. It is one thing for an arrogant necromancer to contact a few spirits and torment them. It's another to engage in ongoing predatory behavior and enslavement of the dead willy nilly.<br /> <br /> It's like the real world. The community and police tolerate a certain level of crime, but once it gets out of hand or cops get shot, then the hammer comes down and people accept whatever is necessary to restore order.<br /> <br /> So I think the Giovanni work within limits that the Hierarchy can accept. Maybe there is some small payoff with Drones, moliated criminals, or captured Spectres, but on terms the Hierarchy can accept.<br /> <br /> Of course, individual Necropoli are different. Some have more resources and others less. Some have good leadership and others bad ones. So Giovanni in one city can get away with more than those in another. But even here if things get out of hand, then the bigger Necropoli or even Stygia sends the necessary reinforcements to restore order.<br /> <br /> In times of great crisis, like during Great Maelstroms, this may fall apart and the Giovanni take advantage, but I think those times are the exception and not the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T23:11:13-07:00","id":856293,"title":"","content":"I think the Giovanni are just slackers, or only paying lip service to the whole &quot;collect a million wraiths&quot; thing (and we all know White Wolf was bad at maths), because an estimated 150,000 people die <i>per day</i> in the real world - and surely that number is higher in the World of Darkness. If only 10% of those that die become wraiths (15,000), and only 10% of those are in Stygian held territories (1500), and we evenly split those between Wraiths, Drones, and Spectres (500 each), then assume that the Giovanni are specifically skimming solely Wraiths off that number, the Necromancers could easily take 20, 30, 50 souls in a 24-hour period. Hell, the Hierarchy might even <i>thank</i> them for taking some off their hands. The (L)egions of the Dead are ever-growing, because except for vampires and a few Arch-Mages, nobody's <b>not</b> dying.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> (As an aside, if the Giovanni were capturing 20 Wraiths a night, consistently, somehow, they would be a little over their one million mark in a little less than 14 years(!). Slackers, I'm telling you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T01:37:09-07:00","id":856339,"title":"","content":"20 out of 500 is 4%. That is a noticeable decrease in tithe to Stygia, and, imho, enough to intervene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:38:43-07:00","id":856407,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that nowhere near 10% of everyone who dies every day becomes a Wraith. Not even 1%, really. But even so, nothing makes a pretty strong point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:51:34-07:00","id":856436,"title":"","content":"I'd argue the reason they haven't already reached a million wraiths for the Final Night ritual is several fold. First, they need to be able to actually keep those wraiths enslaved/imprisoned. There are well south of a million Giovanni, and while I cannot recall off the top of my head if there is a mechanical cap on the wraiths they can individually control it seems reasonable that some sort of limiting factor should exist. Thus, they need to gradually increase their Necromantic capacity to the point where they can actually coral a million wraiths. Second, they don't just need one million wraiths between everyone in the clan they need one million wraiths all in a big bin. Most clan members, even under orders the family's hierarchy, are not going to want to donate their personal retainers. Thus wraiths have to be captured specifically to be used in the eventual ritual, which brings us to the last point. If the Giovanni were to suddenly go on a snatching spree to fill up their pens in short order it would almost certainly attract the attention of the Hierarchy, which the elders of the clan know enough not to do. Vampires are immortal, they can wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:17:07-07:00","id":856569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=856407#post856407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that nowhere near 10% of everyone who dies every day becomes a Wraith. Not even 1%, really. But even so, nothing makes a pretty strong point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another fun numbers game. <br /> <br /> Assume the min. WP to become a wraith is the same as the min. WP to BE a wraith (as opposed to a Drone or Specter with innate WP below 5, but those guys don't really matter so much for gedankenexperiment on the number of wraiths being produced), Which is 5.<br /> <br /> According to Werewolf Delirium chart that's 37% of the population. (For WP 5-10). <br /> <br /> You have to ballpark how many people don't immediately &quot;Transcend&quot; or descend into Oblivion to the point of obliteration, are of the fraction with a WP 5 or over that still become specters, reincarnate immediately or whatever. But there's nothing to indicate that's the vast majority of people who die in Skinlands-adjacent to the Dark Kingdom of Iron go those ways. Being really generous say that's half of all of them, that's still 19% of all deaths could become wraiths. Even if it's just 10% don't Transcend, et al., it's around 4% of all deaths. The number could be more like 25%-30% of all deaths are likely to pop out a wraith.<br /> <br /> Figure out how many deaths there are in Stygian controlled territory per day. Have fun with that. <br /> <br /> Multiply with whatever % you want based on your above choices. <br /> <br /> That's a lot of wraiths per day. Then start calculating how many there have been in the relevant area that could be interpreted as &quot;Stygia&quot; as it's expanded since, arguably Myceanaean times, though, probably since the start Hellenistic/early Roman times. Take out the attrition for succumbing to Oblivion (by whatever means), being turned into dry goods of one sort or another, etc.<br /> <br /> The numbers will start getting frightening very fast. The Dark Kingdom could easily encompass a population of hundreds of millions or even over a billion functioning wraiths. Even if the attrition is REALLY high, it's just going to slide the scale towards the lower end of that range. <br /> <br /> That being the case, the Giovanni probably don't stand much of a chance if they try to start a head-on war through invasion. Probably why that isn't at all what they are trying to do... Isn't the 1 million sous for the Grand Ritual to drop the Shroud and merge the worlds of the living and the dead? Not so sure the Giovanni would fare so well in that situation either, but that is a completely different discussion. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:57:03-07:00","id":856598,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5238_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5238\" data-vbnamecard=\"5238\">Herbert_West</a> That's 4% of the autonomous Wraiths, though. I would think the Legions lose more than that to Renegade and Heretic &quot;recruitment&quot; (and a Giovanni-enslaved Wraith is one that doesn't drift to those organizations, so might be considered less of a problem, depending). The Hierarchy would still be Reaping (most) of those 500 Drones, as well. Then again, that 15k people don't all die in one place, so there would be unique local factors to consider. Like, New York - if the Giovanni take 50 Wraiths a day, I don't think the Legions would be too upset, but a smaller town they might (and Auggie help the Giovanni that snatches a soul the Legion has been waiting on).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2082\" data-vbnamecard=\"2082\">Schleiermacher</a> I <i>think</i> it's a conflated bit from <i>W2e</i> on my part, and not an exact measurement, but more of a guideline. Using the Fog chart, which gives a breakdown of the average Willpower per population, 10% of people have Willpower 10, and that was the metric I used. Not perfect, admittedly, but nice round numbers, and since the core book notes that (usually) only persons with extraordinary (W)illpower become Wraiths, I didn't include the percentages from Willpower 7-9. I'm sure that the percentage of dead becoming Wraiths per day varies, but I like easy round numbers and averages. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> Oh yeah, what I'm saying is John Giovanni needs to capture 20 Wraiths a night for 14 years, John and Bob Giovanni need to each capture 10 Wraiths a night for 14 years, that kind of thing. The Giovnanni as an entity have been around for close to 500 years, and they only got close to their one million mark somewhat recently? What, were they only working weekends? One Necromancer needs to capture 1 Wraith a night for 280 years to hit their mark. The Clan, as a body, are slackers, and I'm gonna mock them for it. They're slack-ass slackers from slackingtown. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:03:22-07:00","id":856603,"title":"","content":"Writing at the same time as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> was posting.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=856569#post856569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably why that isn't at all what they are trying to do... Isn't the 1 million sous for the Grand Ritual to drop the Shroud and merge the worlds of the living and the dead? Not so sure the Giovanni would fare so well in that situation either, but that is a completely different discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's the idiot plan. &quot;Hey, let's drop the Shroud and merge the worlds! We'll be god-kings because we can control a handful of ghosts, and everyone else will be <i>so scared</i>! Woo!&quot; I'm actually surprised that some of the Deathlords aren't just shoving more Wraiths at the Giovanni to make that happen, Yu Haung at least. &quot;Yes, yes, make that happen, drop the Shroud... nothing but us poor lonely little ghosts over here...&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 03-31-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T11:42:52-07:00","id":856622,"title":"","content":"Why would the Hierarchy care about a million bound wraiths? The leadership have probably used more than that to construct summer homes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=855787#post855787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Wraith game (and only Wraith game) I ever ran was set in a small-town Necropolis in northern Louisiana. The problem was that of the few residents, some were beginning to vanish. The players had time to discover it was the work of a vampiric necromancer living in a trailer park on the edge of town before one of the players got a new job schedule and the game ended. Vamps make for fun antagonists, but you really have to tweak their stats or they just don't interact with Wraiths that much unless they have MAD dots of Necromancy and TONS of Rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the way necromancers are portrayed in Wraith supplements, it seems to assume that most of them are walking around with four or five dots in at least one Path. The actual ability of a made-with-chargen-rules Giovanni to coerce and bind wraiths is nowhere near the capabilities that the fiction posits them as having. <i>Mediums </i>and others seem to imagine that the typical necromancer has capacities that are many dots deep into Necromantic Paths and that these powers are very reliable - but this definitely isn't the case of a typical Vampire character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=856603#post856603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Writing at the same time as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> was posting.Yep, that's the idiot plan. &quot;Hey, let's drop the Shroud and merge the worlds! We'll be god-kings because we can control a handful of ghosts, and everyone else will be <i>so scared</i>! Woo!&quot; I'm actually surprised that some of the Deathlords aren't just shoving more Wraiths at the Giovanni to make that happen, Yu Huang at least. &quot;Yes, yes, make that happen, drop the Shroud... nothing but us poor lonely little ghosts over here...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that may just be Voormas's plan working as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:20:19-07:00","id":856715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=856598#post856598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> Oh yeah, what I'm saying is John Giovanni needs to capture 20 Wraiths a night for 14 years, John and Bob Giovanni need to each capture 10 Wraiths a night for 14 years, that kind of thing. The Giovnanni as an entity have been around for close to 500 years, and they only got close to their one million mark somewhat recently? What, were they only working weekends? One Necromancer needs to capture 1 Wraith a night for 280 years to hit their mark. The Clan, as a body, are slackers, and I'm gonna mock them for it. They're slack-ass slackers from slackingtown. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually if I'm remembering the Revised Giovanni Clanbook correctly, they'd managed to capture something like 28 million of the necessary <i><b>100</b></i> million wraiths for the Endless Night ritual by the time the Sixth Great Maelstrom hit in '99 and made their Shadowland gulags go kablooey. Indications were that was thanks to half a millennium of collaborative effort by the vampires on the living side of the Shroud and allied Giovanni family wraiths skulking around and kidnapping people on the dead side. Their plan was supposedly to get to half the needed amount and then crash the world economy and trigger a World War to scoop up the other 50 million all at once, though clearly that plan didn't take into account how disruptive a maelstrom would be to their ghostly resources and allies. Bear in mind, this was also a ritual with a suspiciously round number requirement that was invented by a batshit crazy vampire, who expected to diablerize <i>God</i> once the Shroud came down.<br /> <br /> I can't recall if I read the criticism of the plan in a book or if someone posted it here, but I've seen it pointed out that the Giovanni also possess Dominate and can make living humans their puppets on an individual level comparable to necromantic binding, yet curiously have not managed to take over the world in the past 500 years. Their assumption that they would be able to do so almost immediately once it's merged with the netherworld plainly hasn't been subjected to a thorough peer review.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 03-31-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T14:40:04-07:00","id":856722,"title":"","content":"It's all Voormas' fault. All of it.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine quite a few Malfeans, Deathlords and Yama Kings are aiding and abetting him from their side of the Shroud too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T16:39:39-07:00","id":857337,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3505_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3505\" data-vbnamecard=\"3505\">Matt the Bruins fan</a> One <i>hundred</i> million?! Well, that's a little different, then. A million's just a rounding error at that point. Still gonna call them slackers, though.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T06:03:04-07:00","id":858300,"title":"","content":"I am pretty sure that one million is not an end goal. Hundred million is. I originally posted an estimation, that GIovanni already got around million.<br /> <br /> But the WW math is bad anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=856622#post856622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the way necromancers are portrayed in Wraith supplements, it seems to assume that most of them are walking around with four or five dots in at least one Path. The actual ability of a made-with-chargen-rules Giovanni to coerce and bind wraiths is nowhere near the capabilities that the fiction posits them as having. <i>Mediums </i>and others seem to imagine that the typical necromancer has capacities that are many dots deep into Necromantic Paths and that these powers are very reliable - but this definitely isn't the case of a typical Vampire character.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have a reverse problem with portraying wraiths and spectres. They have to be crazy strong, to be useful/dangerous.<br /> I always assume that spectres in my Vampire games are some kind old elite guys, because they need Shroud Rending 4-5 just to see my characters. And a lot more to actually hurt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","user":"LordOfCinder","date":". 04-03-2016, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:15:18-07:00","id":858389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=858300#post858300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am pretty sure that one million is not an end goal. Hundred million is. I originally posted an estimation, that GIovanni already got around million.<br /> <br /> But the WW math is bad anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually have a reverse problem with portraying wraiths and spectres. They have to be crazy strong, to be useful/dangerous.<br /> I always assume that spectres in my Vampire games are some kind old elite guys, because they need Shroud Rending 4-5 just to see my characters. And a lot more to actually hurt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are your vampires using some badass necromancy to make them wraith-invisible or high levels of Obfuscate? Otherwise, there's no reason ANY wraith couldn't see a vampire in the Skinlands. It would be about as hard as seeing any person, tree, car, wall, etc. Then they could use relatively low levels of Outrage to toss them around like pillows while the vamps couldn't attack back at all (again, without bad ass levels of Necromancy of some sort). A normal-sized circle of Dictum-non-compliant Renegades or Heretics at the low-ish end of the ability using forbidden Arcanoi could cause a vampire coterie or pack some serious problems (wait until daylight and then there are all sorts of things they could do to &quot;introduce&quot; the vampires to sunlight). <br /> <br /> Specters would be another matter, unless, say, they were Doppelgangers, in which case they're pretty much the same as wraiths. Specters of other sorts have issues outside of the Tempest and would have to be pretty powerful to be a consistent threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:19:03-07:00","id":858525,"title":"","content":"Spectres have spectre cults, too, of course. They needn't attack you directly. And there are literally *so many* spectres, there are going to be some with Shroud Rending.<br /> <br /> Spectres will probably leave necromancers alone unless the necromancers bother them first. At which point, the spectres can call for aid through the Hive Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:47:14-07:00","id":859787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=858389#post858389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are your vampires using some badass necromancy to make them wraith-invisible or high levels of Obfuscate? Otherwise, there's no reason ANY wraith couldn't see a vampire in the Skinlands. It would be about as hard as seeing any person, tree, car, wall, etc. Then they could use relatively low levels of Outrage to toss them around like pillows while the vamps couldn't attack back at all (again, without bad ass levels of Necromancy of some sort). A normal-sized circle of Dictum-non-compliant Renegades or Heretics at the low-ish end of the ability using forbidden Arcanoi could cause a vampire coterie or pack some serious problems (wait until daylight and then there are all sorts of things they could do to &quot;introduce&quot; the vampires to sunlight).<br /> <br /> Specters would be another matter, unless, say, they were Doppelgangers, in which case they're pretty much the same as wraiths. Specters of other sorts have issues outside of the Tempest and would have to be pretty powerful to be a consistent threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didnt know doppelgangers had life sight. Thank you very much, it clears a lot of stuff for me.<br /> However, EVERYONE keep offering wraith introduces vampire to daylight situation. Question is, what use this scene will be if it Kills all of my players characters=)<br /> <br /> I also have to importnat question. How does Wraith LOOK like when his caul is still intact?<br /> And how do relics appear, and what kind of cool relics besides weapons can wraith possess?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T16:43:09-07:00","id":859970,"title":"","content":"Did you miss &quot;toss them around with Outrage&quot;? Do your vampires have the ability to touch wraiths? If not, it's a very upsetting fight for the vampires. Especially if there's a broken broom handle lying around. Try to get ANYTHING done if a master of Pandemonium is cutting loose. Even Celerity gets weird when space is getting bent. (Run very very quickly down the endless corridor that does an ouroborous). And so and so on.<br /> <br /> Like a person in whispy cocoon. <br /> <br /> How about a car? A shoe? A teddy bear? A ballpoint pen (that might actually work!)? Anything anyone could ever have cared about deeply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T15:21:29-07:00","id":860586,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that being forcibly discorporated by being hit with a weapon, object, or fist costs a ghostly being a point of Corpus. Vampires who aren't adept necromancers do, in fact, still have the ability to fight back physically although it's a pale shadow of how effective they are against a living or undead opponent. Still, powers that render them largely invulnerable to harm, such as high levels of Fortitude, Protean, and Obtenebration, are probably as common among vampires as high levels of Outrage are among wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T16:59:40-07:00","id":860645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860586#post860586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that being forcibly discorporated by being hit with a weapon, object, or fist costs a ghostly being a point of Corpus. Vampires who aren't adept necromancers do, in fact, still have the ability to fight back physically although it's a pale shadow of how effective they are against a living or undead opponent. Still, powers that render them largely invulnerable to harm, such as high levels of Fortitude, Protean, and Obtenebration, are probably as common among vampires as high levels of Outrage are among wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discorporation lasts [Stamina] turns. So it's one Corpus every few turns maximum. It's hardly much of a danger.<br /> <br /> Most wraiths are sensible enough to dodge out the way of Skinlands objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T18:50:14-07:00","id":860703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860586#post860586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that being forcibly discorporated by being hit with a weapon, object, or fist costs a ghostly being a point of Corpus. Vampires who aren't adept necromancers do, in fact, still have the ability to fight back physically although it's a pale shadow of how effective they are against a living or undead opponent. Still, powers that render them largely invulnerable to harm, such as high levels of Fortitude, Protean, and Obtenebration, are probably as common among vampires as high levels of Outrage are among wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they can't SEE their opponents without Auspex. And arguably not all that easily with that. So they need to find the wraith, who, by the way can be standing across the room chucking heavy things at the vampire. Which might be pretty far away for the vamp if the Spook has a Haunter buddy with Tempus Fugit. <br /> <br /> The point is not that vamps can't stand up to wraiths. The point is that the statement that only really powerful wraiths can have any effect on vampires (other than just arranging for a session of sunbathing) is simply not true. At relatively similar levels of power, a wraith group the focuses on affecting the Skinlands can be a serious annoyance to a coterie of vampires and the vampires will have a substantially hard time really being AS annoying back without being able to, say, find their Fetters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:44:11-07:00","id":860896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860703#post860703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they can't SEE their opponents without Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex dont normally let you see ghosts. Its more of a &quot;on storytellers discretion&quot;<br /> <br /> I have one more question(the more I read the more I get), can or can't you use Keening across the Shroud? It seems unclear in the rule book, but in Vampire sample ghosts have Dementation like powers, which I figured IS Keening.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T03:41:28-07:00","id":860917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860896#post860896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex dont normally let you see ghosts. Its more of a &amp;quot;on storytellers discretion&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I have one more question(the more I read the more I get), can or can't you use Keening across the Shroud? It seems unclear in the rule book, but in Vampire sample ghosts have Dementation like powers, which I figured IS Keening.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. You'd probably need a tempered Arcanos, as humans can't hear you otherwise. A relaxed ST might just allow it though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T07:39:23-07:00","id":861031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860896#post860896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026can or can't you use Keening across the Shroud? It seems unclear in the rule book, but in Vampire sample ghosts have Dementation like powers, which I figured IS Keening.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Some of the mechanics [in Second Edition] make me think that it can affect mortals.<br /> <br /> From <i>Dirge</i> (p. 146): \u201cFive successes will affect a mortal with a negative emotion for a week. Wraiths, however, are not as affected.\u201d<br /> <br /> From <i>Ballad</i> (p. 146): \u201cFive successes can flood a mortal with cheer for an entire week. Wraiths are less easily cajoled\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> From <i>Muse</i> (p. 147): \u201cThis art works equally well on wraiths, mortals, and other supernatural beings.\u201d<br /> <br /> From <i>Crescendo</i> (p. 147): \u201cSinging a Crescendo while Embodied inflicts listeners\u2026one Health Level of damage per two successes.\u201d<br /> This mechanic specfically states that wraith needs to be Embodied to affect the other side of the Shroud.<br /> <br /> <i>Requiem</i> doesn\u2019t have anything for or against using it across the Shroud. I\u2019d be inclined to say that it does; it\u2019s a really cool ghostly power.<br /> <br /> Of course, this could all change in Wr20.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:52:59-07:00","id":861154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860896#post860896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex dont normally let you see ghosts. Its more of a &quot;on storytellers discretion&quot;<br /> <br /> I have one more question(the more I read the more I get), can or can't you use Keening across the Shroud? It seems unclear in the rule book, but in Vampire sample ghosts have Dementation like powers, which I figured IS Keening.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My V20 ST Screen clearly has a Wraith (intermittent, faint aura) line. So I think it's a lock that Auspex 2 can see them. Seems like it might be a more difficult than normal targeting sense. Like the person had occasional cover (shooting someone running through the trees, for example). And, oh, that Diff 8 to even use the power sucks. but it's definitely there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T22:38:02-07:00","id":861606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=860917#post860917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question. You'd probably need a tempered Arcanos, as humans can't hear you otherwise. A relaxed ST might just allow it though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraith: The Great War has the following in its Keening writeup (specifically under Dirge, on p. 120):<br /> <br /> Note that while mortals within &quot;earshot&quot; of the Chanteur are affected by Keening, the Quick cannot actually <i>hear</i> the Chanteur unless the wraith uses Embody or some similar art to make his voice audible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:28:33-07:00","id":861949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=861606#post861606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wraith: The Great War has the following in its Keening writeup (specifically under Dirge, on p. 120):<br /> <br /> Note that while mortals within &amp;quot;earshot&amp;quot; of the Chanteur are affected by Keening, the Quick cannot actually <i>hear</i> the Chanteur unless the wraith uses Embody or some similar art to make his voice audible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect! That makes sense. Keening is quite a powerful Arcanos, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T02:28:47-07:00","id":865376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=861154#post861154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My V20 ST Screen clearly has a Wraith (intermittent, faint aura) line. So I think it's a lock that Auspex 2 can see them. Seems like it might be a more difficult than normal targeting sense. Like the person had occasional cover (shooting someone running through the trees, for example). And, oh, that Diff 8 to even use the power sucks. but it's definitely there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it relates to Risen or Embodied wraiths that Vampire can see anyway. If Auspex 2 would give such an awareness, there would be much more Necromancer clans.<br /> <br /> On a side note, Kindred of Ebony Kindred had the alternate system for Auspex 1, where you can see spirits on 5 successes. Which was clearly written as a unique, different way of utilizing Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T10:08:07-07:00","id":865566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=865376#post865376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it relates to Risen or Embodied wraiths that Vampire can see anyway. If Auspex 2 would give such an awareness, there would be much more Necromancer clans.<br /> <br /> On a side note, Kindred of Ebony Kindred had the alternate system for Auspex 1, where you can see spirits on 5 successes. Which was clearly written as a unique, different way of utilizing Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the way you want to run it, then go ahead, but V20 doesn't seem to agree with you. Check out Aura Perception (p. 135-136) in conjunction with Seeing the Unseen (p.142). There is nothing to indicate that the ghost has to be visible, in fact, according to seeing the unseen, it definitely can be invisible to normal sight. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure why having ghosts visible to Auspex would have any effect on Necromancy paths anymore then being able to see magic around mages would have any effect on Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T23:59:10-07:00","id":865827,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I just want to put forward that I've never read a Wraith book. All my info about Wraith is from internet sources like the various Wiki's and this forum.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I actually asked a similar question to this a while back on these boards. It was more a general topic of how Vampires and Wraiths might interact. The topic also had some discussion about how easy it was to cross the two games over. Both for PC/PC crossovers and using the either Vamps or Wraiths as NPC's in the other game line. Inevitably this turned to talk about Vampire Necromancers interacting with Wraiths. Link below: <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372242-dead-and-deader-vampire-and-wraith-interaction\">Dead and Deader - Vampire and Wraith Interactions</a></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The level to which Vampires with Necromancy interact with Wraith society has been something I've been trying to figure out (one of the reason I created the above topic) since I first started reading up about Wraith during the Wr20 Kickstarter.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I think its fair to say that the two game lines do not mesh perfectly. With the CWoD being originally built as (mostly) distinct settings for each game-line making it hard from the start. Add the fact Wraith never got a Revised Edition and it all gets pretty sticky and unreliable in general. It could be argued that the Wraith side of the fluff is &quot;out of date&quot; in regards to Vampiric interactions with the Revised Edition fluff. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">On top of this at least some of the game sources that do provide information on this topic are written from an in-character/in-universe point of view. As such they are supposed to be biased and unreliable. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Short Answer:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> Read what limited, bias and arguable out-dated fluff there is on the topic. Make up your own mind how Vampiric Necromancers factor into Wraith and how Wraiths (and their fluff) factor into your Vampire games.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Alternatively, hold off to after Wr20 and hope its got some new info. Even if it turns out to be a handful of paragraphs. Its still perhaps going to be new info (or a new take on old info) that you could use to decide.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Really Long Answer:</b><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As far as I know with Wraith being cut off at the end of 2nd Edition it only really talks about three different groups of Kindred Necromancers:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">1) The Giovanni</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2) The Samedi</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">3) The Nagaraja</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Giovanni:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Other posters have pretty much covered the default Giovanni fluff and stance in this instance I feel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">They are dicks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The majority of the Clan treat Wraiths like tools and slaves. From their point of view they are the masters of the Dead. From Stygia's point of view they are small fry it seems.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Personally, the Giovanni are perhaps my least favourite Clan. Their fluff is with the exception of a few recent additions is terrible. V20 Rites of Blood and V20DA add some stuff to them that finally managed to make them passingly interesting to me. I have yet to read their V20 Lore of the Clans entry, so maybe that will add something too them as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So basically I'm bias against them. <br /> <br /> Meaning that <b>IF</b> I included them in a Wraith game I'd likely have an NPC Giovanni that was against type (actually friendly towards Wraiths, or at least reasonable). Likewise, I'd likely downplay their level of involvement in Wraithly affairs and make it very clear they have no real clue as to what is really going on with the Underworld.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Samedi:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm actually very interested in Wraithly perceptions of this Bloodline. As they claim to have the patronage of Baron Samedi. I believe there is a group of Wraiths (Les Invisibles) that work for or are tied to the Loa as well. So I could see some interesting crossover material coming out of that.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">If anyone does know more on this topic or has featured Samedi in their games I'd appreciate it. As its a really interesting bit of fluff I think.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Nagaraja:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">One of my favourite bloodlines. So like the Giovanni case I'm a little bias, though in the opposite way. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The older members where mortal Death Mages obsessed with exploring and harnessing the power of the Underworld before they were Vampires. They found Enoch about 2500 years ago (at least) and have hung out there on and off for that whole time. Its safe to say they likely know a whole hell of a lot more about the Underworld then any other Vampires. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">However, there are maybe around 100 of these guys in the world. Likely a third (at least) of them at least are located in Enoch at any one time. Most Vampires don't know about these guys. So I can't imagine they are well known enough in Wraith society to have a prevailing opinion on them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> I can see the Tal'Mahe'Ra Wraiths obviously working for and allied to them. Likely some occult expert Wraiths and high ups in Stygia likely know about them.Other then that I can see them being a sort of &quot;Urban Legend&quot; in Wraith society. A type of undead necromancer who can EAT Wraiths, can take physical form in the Skinlands and can control the energies of Oblivion? Talk about the boogie man. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Consider that the Nagaraja eat flesh rather then drink blood. Also consider that the Underworld lacks the Sun, normal fire and trees. So its unlikely that any of the traditional Vampire weaknesses are likely to show up. I think its plausible given all this that its not obvious to a Wraith a Nagaraja is even a Vampire. Could be some weird plasmid creature from the Tempest, or a really, really odd type of Risen or Mage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">After that you run into the Kindred Necromancers that were never covered by Wraith. Mainly because they were added to Vampire after the Wraith line ended:<br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> 1) The Cappadocians<br /> 2) The Lamia,<br /> 3) Mla Watu <br /> 4) Impundulu<br /> 5)The Harbingers of Skulls <br /> <br /> (The last four are all Bloodlines off of the Cappadocians, expect the Impundulu...maybe.)<br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">So you have to make up your own stuff. Well, at least for now as Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, Lore of the Bloodlines for V20 along with Tome of Secrets V20DA might help with this. Also of course Wr20 itself might mention and comment on them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Here is my take on them:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Cappadocians:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'd say with the exception of maybe Cappadocius himself the &quot;Clan of Death&quot; are likely just as clueless to the Underworld as their Giovanni successors. As the point of the Giovanni getting embraced into the Cappadocian Clan was to give the access to Ghost/Shadowland Necromancy basically.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Lamia:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Lamia likely knew as little about Wraiths and the Underworld as their Cappadocian patrons. That being said you have a bit more wiggle room for interpretation with them. Since all the odd Lilith knowledge and sorcery going on with them means they theoretically &quot;could&quot; know more. That's not really supported or mentioned in their fluff though so YMMV on that one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Mla Watu:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">If I remember correctly (its been ages since I read KotEK) these guys are supposed to be pretty fascinated by the unique Underworld of Africa, namely the Dark Kingdom of Ivory. So they likely understand how things work in that Kingdom better then any other Kindred Necromancers. <br /> <br /> They also came up with their own path of Necromancy that the Giovanni eventually stole called the Cenotaph Path. Which is all about interacting with a Wraiths fetters and sensing how close the Underworld is to the living world. So a pretty good Path for Crossover play really (more so then any other Kindred Necromancer save maybe Samedi). I'd say they likely have a solid understanding of Wraiths, though a Dark Kingdom of Ivory cultural filter at least. <br /> <br /> <b>Impundulu:</b><br /> <br /> New bloodline only included in V20DA for the first time. Fluff has it that they are mainly concerned with the balancing of life and death in the living world. So I doubt they know much about the Underworld. Due to said focus they like the Mla Watu often practice the Cenotaph Path. However, they also have access to the Path of Haunting, which mainly effects living people, but the final power allows them to make it easier for Wraiths to effect certain people. So I'd say they have a pretty good understanding of Wraiths when it comes to Wraiths interactions with the living world. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Harbingers of Skulls:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I would expect the Harbingers to know a lot more then the Giovanni but likely less then the Nagaraja.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Their origin is basically they are normal Cappadocians who get sealed into the Underworld by their Antediluvian. So I suspect their education about the Underworld and Wraithly society was rather &quot;do or die (again)&quot;. School of hard knocks indeed. Some of them survived to form the Bloodline and get out of the Underworld 500+ years later.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Personally I can't see them doing that without getting at least some help from at least one Wraithly faction. They likely owe someone a lot of favours and likely made a fair few enemies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The issue with them at current is that its not clear how &quot;deep&quot; in the Underworld they were trapped. Some of the fluff suggests &quot;merely&quot; them being trapped in the Shadowlands. Other fluff suggests something closer to the Sunless Sea/Tempest. Hopefully Lore of the Bloodlines will expand on their fluff and clear this up.<br /> <br /> <b>Final thoughts:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What I would stress with any Kindred Necromancer interacting with Wraiths is the individual differences of said Necromancer. Their are likely stereotypes about Vampiric Necromancers in Wraith Society no doubt. To the more well informed Wraith there are likely even stereotypes for the different Clans and Bloodlines that use Necromancy. Ultimately though all such Necromancers are going to be individually different.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A lot of the Kindred Clans and Bloodlines with access to Necromancy have strong &quot;solitary figure&quot; aspects, in particular the Harbingers and Nagaraja. The Samedi are do have a good Bloodline unity but they are still rare. Even the Giovanni, despite working for &quot;the good of the family&quot; have their own wheeling-and-dealing to manage and cultivate.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'd say its fine to have the sterotype among Wraiths of:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i><b>&quot;Vampires are asshats. Vampiric Necromancers are even bigger asshats. The Giovanni are of course the biggest asshats of all.&quot;</b></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">However, I'd say once you've planted that seed among your PC's and cultivated it with a dickish minor Vampire NPC enjoy subverting it: <br /> <br /> Introduce a genuinely likable and useful NPC Kindred Necromancer (any Clan or Bloodline with Necromancy) that the PC's can gain as a contact or even ally. <br /> <br /> Throw in an Elder Nagaraja NPC who they &quot;could&quot; make an enemy of to terrify the hell out of your PC group if they get overconfident about dealing with Vampires.<br /> <br /> Have a powerful figure in one of the Legions the PC's interact with have a Harbinger &quot;retainer&quot; that owes him/her and is instructed to &quot;help&quot; the group (read - keep an eye on them).<br /> <br /> Right done...sorry that was so long a post. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T10:34:02-07:00","id":866003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=865827#post865827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#222222][FONT=arial]<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Harbingers of Skulls:</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I would expect the Harbingers to know a lot more then the Giovanni but likely less then the Nagaraja.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Their origin is basically they are normal Cappadocians who get sealed into the Underworld by their Antediluvian. So I suspect their education about the Underworld and Wraithly society was rather &quot;do or die (again)&quot;. School of hard knocks indeed. Some of them survived to form the Bloodline and get out of the Underworld 500+ years later.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Personally I can't see them doing that without getting at least some help from at least one Wraithly faction. They likely owe someone a lot of favours and likely made a fair few enemies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The issue with them at current is that its not clear how &quot;deep&quot; in the Underworld they were trapped. Some of the fluff suggests &quot;merely&quot; them being trapped in the Shadowlands. Other fluff suggests something closer to the Sunless Sea/Tempest. Hopefully Lore of the Bloodlines will expand on their fluff and clear this up.<br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra has it that the Harbringers effectively split in two; those who stayed where they'd been trapped in the Shadowlands, bent on getting out and getting revenge, became the Sabbat's Harbringers, while another group ventured into the Tempest, where they discovered Enoch and the Tal'Mahe'Ra; they're not particularly concerned with revenge, pursuing other goals instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:24:21-07:00","id":866050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=866003#post866003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra has it that the Harbringers effectively split in two; those who stayed where they'd been trapped in the Shadowlands, bent on getting out and getting revenge, became the Sabbat's Harbringers, while another group ventured into the Tempest, where they discovered Enoch and the Tal'Mahe'Ra; they're not particularly concerned with revenge, pursuing other goals instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, they're also playing all sides off against each other, as per the motivations of the Cult of the Capuchin. So it's quite possible that both the Sabbat Harbingers and the TMR branch are a lot more aligned than the Sabbat or TMR realises.<br /> <br /> Remember, too, that necromancy of all kinds has been tainted by Voormas, and so all necromancers, at some level, seem to want to merge the worlds of the living and dead to allow Voormas to stop the Wheel. Positioning themselves in Enoch would give them opportunities to help seek that goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T14:28:37-07:00","id":866120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, too, that necromancy of all kinds has been tainted by Voormas </div> </div> </div>Mmmm...wasn't that part of the fluff of Time of Judgement that wasn't strictly canon?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:18:44-07:00","id":866691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=866120#post866120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmm...wasn't that part of the fluff of Time of Judgement that wasn't strictly canon?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorta. It was built up to and alluded to in other supplements, and was obviously a guiding principle for the developers, as so many necromantic groups across the gamelines are/were obsessed with tearing down the Shroud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T11:16:33-07:00","id":868590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=865566#post865566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that's the way you want to run it, then go ahead, but V20 doesn't seem to agree with you. Check out Aura Perception (p. 135-136) in conjunction with Seeing the Unseen (p.142). There is nothing to indicate that the ghost has to be visible, in fact, according to seeing the unseen, it definitely can be invisible to normal sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, damn. If you are right - that changes everything. Auspex is VERY common discipline, and even Clans that don't normally have it - can have access to few levels relatively easy.<br /> <br /> It breaks all logic that non Necromancer Kindred know NOTHING about ghosts and don't interact with them often,if Auspex 2 lets you see them. Also all that system, Giovanni spy on Camarilla using ghosts - stops working immediately.<br /> <br /> I have a Giovanni character with no Necromancy, but out of clan Auspex. And me and the players were pretty sure you won't see ghosts. I am confused.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5748-lordofcinder","name":"LordOfCinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:01:14-07:00","id":868740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfCinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=868590#post868590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, damn. If you are right - that changes everything. Auspex is VERY common discipline, and even Clans that don't normally have it - can have access to few levels relatively easy.<br /> <br /> It breaks all logic that non Necromancer Kindred know NOTHING about ghosts and don't interact with them often,if Auspex 2 lets you see them. Also all that system, Giovanni spy on Camarilla using ghosts - stops working immediately.<br /> <br /> I have a Giovanni character with no Necromancy, but out of clan Auspex. And me and the players were pretty sure you won't see ghosts. I am confused.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of latitude in what that description ends up meaning. Turning on Aura sight and getting a few photo negative images of pale smears that stutter their way across a room isn't really the same as what would be seen if a wraith could use Embody to appear. It's more like being able to see someone's shadow, but not the person casting it, while the lights keep going on and off. You can have it take several successes to even get much of a bead on a wraith, particularly if they are moving around. Or there are several of them around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T19:09:53-07:00","id":868994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=868740#post868740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a lot of latitude in what that description ends up meaning. Turning on Aura sight and getting a few photo negative images of pale smears that stutter their way across a room isn't really the same as what would be seen if a wraith could use Embody to appear. It's more like being able to see someone's shadow, but not the person casting it, while the lights keep going on and off. You can have it take several successes to even get much of a bead on a wraith, particularly if they are moving around. Or there are several of them around.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I interpreted it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T20:46:18-07:00","id":869070,"title":"","content":"I had always assumed <i>Vampire</i>'s Auspex Aura Perception chart was used for Wraiths who are using Embody, or Puppetry, or even Inhabit - <s>or are Risen</s>, rather than just &quot;present,&quot; as the text says Vampires must stare at the target &quot;for at least a few seconds.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot that Risen auras present themselves the same as Vampire auras. Oops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 04-20-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T03:00:53-07:00","id":869198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=869070#post869070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had always assumed <i>Vampire</i>'s Auspex Aura Perception chart was used for Wraiths who are using Embody, or Puppetry, or even Inhabit - <s>or are Risen</s>, rather than just &amp;quot;present,&amp;quot; as the text says Vampires must stare at the target &amp;quot;for at least a few seconds.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot that Risen auras present themselves the same as Vampire auras. Oops.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm reading it right, first you have to see the unseen. Then you can see their aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T07:54:43-07:00","id":869315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=869070#post869070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had always assumed <i>Vampire</i>'s Auspex Aura Perception chart was used for Wraiths who are using Embody, or Puppetry, or even Inhabit - <s>or are Risen</s>, rather than just &quot;present,&quot; as the text says Vampires must stare at the target &quot;for at least a few seconds.&quot;<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot that Risen auras present themselves the same as Vampire auras. Oops.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the Seeing the Unseen box in V20. Since it has that name and specifically addresses wraiths, it's pretty much a lock that Embody isn't needed. Puppetry and Inhabit present different issues. As it's not a wraith book, it doesn't deal with it Arcanos by Arcanos. <br /> <br /> I'd probably go with some &quot;ersatz common sense&quot; benchmarks. <br /> Wraiths not interacting with the Skinlands register as per above, whether using Arcanoi or not.<br /> Embody - You see what Embody shows with a constant pale flickering aura as per a normal Aura Sight<br /> Puppetry - The wraithly aura suppresses the normal one. Vamps can pick out the possessed fairly easily<br /> Inhabit - Same as Puppetry, but vamps may not notice with a &quot;crowd read&quot; as they don't really look for auras of objects... Alternatively that might make use of Inhabit stand out.... &quot;Why does that car have an aura?&quot;<br /> Outrage, Pandemonium, Flux - Probably easier to pin down than the normal stutter-stop. Especially if &quot;caught in the act&quot;<br /> Keening, Phantasm - They probably are somewhat easier to see when they are affecting Skinlands targets.<br /> <br /> I'm just going to stop there and not go to the trouble of seeking out Dark Kingdom or Specter Arcanoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:58:16-07:00","id":869398,"title":"","content":"Huh. It looks like I've skipped over this every read:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is possible, though difficult, to sense the aura of a being who is invisible to normal sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think Aura Perception gave Vampires extra-planar sight, like D&amp;D. In that case does it allow the user to see past the Gauntlet and into the Penumbra and Periphery? Can one see another Vampire using Psychic Projection (and thus also see into the lower Astral Realm)?<br /> <br /> I don't think I like that - the Chakravanti studying the Toreador is no long doing so in secret; the Garou waiting in ambush on the other side of the Gauntlet for the Tzimisce is no longer a surprise*. I think I'll stick with &quot;Aura Perception reads the 'energy' emitted by creatures on the same plane/in the same realm&quot; reading.<br /> <br /> I mean, I have allowed players to use Aura Perception to see through Obtenebration's Shroud of Night, mostly because it's a smart tactic (and those deserve to be rewarded), and also because fuck the Lasombra, but those are things that exist on the same planar level.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br /> *Which, given Auspex' &quot;danger sense,&quot; might not have been a surprise anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T12:11:36-07:00","id":869513,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'm not seeing anything in Auspex RAW that suggests that it grants powers of cross-dimensional examination. While it does bestow limited powers of detecting concealment, both natural and preternatural, it excludes seeing (among other things) umbra-traveling werewolves and Shadowland-skulking wraiths. In this case, wraiths aren\u2019t hidden (as discussed in \u201cunseen\u201d); they\u2019re in an entirely different dimension (albeit one that has limited interactions with another realms, i.e., the Skinlands).<br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:57:51-07:00","id":870353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=869513#post869513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'm not seeing anything in Auspex RAW that suggests that it grants powers of cross-dimensional examination. While it does bestow limited powers of detecting concealment, both natural and preternatural, it excludes seeing (among other things) umbra-traveling werewolves and Shadowland-skulking wraiths. In this case, wraiths aren\u2019t hidden (as discussed in \u201cunseen\u201d); they\u2019re in an entirely different dimension (albeit one that has limited interactions with another realms, i.e., the Skinlands).<br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like a really strict reading of the text. If that's what you want, go for it, but absent authorial guidance, it doesn't seem entirely reasonable to construe the word &quot;hidden&quot; to mean &quot;materially present but unable to be seen&quot;. That &quot;materially present&quot; is the part that is not present in the definition of hidden occulted, obfuscated. unssen, etc. It's something you are adding in. In any case, wraiths ARE at least partially materially present but unseen, in any case. Hence the Rule of Ouch, the need to spend Corpus to walk through a wall, etc. Something that is not true for Werewolves in the Penumbra or Mages in the nearby High Umbra. Where it is entirely &quot;look but don't touch, unless you do so in a special magical way.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't take much a stretch to imagine why vampires can't see werewolves in the Penumbra. They're dead. They're already Shadowlands-adjacent. They are not Umbra (in the werewolf sense) adjacent. That's the realm of LIFE. That is backed up in numerous ways. Look at all of Necromancy vs.the limited nature of Spiritus. The fact that both wraiths and vampires have pale auras. Etc. Of course, the whole folderol with Psychic Projection is definitely problematic in this regard, as it really confuses exactly where the Vampire is with regard to the spirit realms of the other supernaturals. Two vamps using Psych Projection can see each other. They can even battle WP to WP. Apparently, ghosts, werewolves and other entities may or may not be able to see projecting vamps, with a lean towards &quot;may&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:17:46-07:00","id":870371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=870353#post870353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems like a really strict reading of the text. If that's what you want, go for it, but absent authorial guidance, it doesn't seem entirely reasonable to construe the word &quot;hidden&quot; to mean &quot;materially present but unable to be seen&quot;. That &quot;materially present&quot; is the part that is not present in the definition of hidden occulted, obfuscated. unssen, etc. It's something you are adding in. In any case, wraiths ARE at least partially materially present but unseen, in any case. Hence the Rule of Ouch, the need to spend Corpus to walk through a wall, etc. Something that is not true for Werewolves in the Penumbra or Mages in the nearby High Umbra. Where it is entirely &quot;look but don't touch, unless you do so in a special magical way.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't take much a stretch to imagine why vampires can't see werewolves in the Penumbra. They're dead. They're already Shadowlands-adjacent. They are not Umbra (in the werewolf sense) adjacent. That's the realm of LIFE. That is backed up in numerous ways. Look at all of Necromancy vs.the limited nature of Spiritus. The fact that both wraiths and vampires have pale auras. Etc. Of course, the whole folderol with Psychic Projection is definitely problematic in this regard, as it really confuses exactly where the Vampire is with regard to the spirit realms of the other supernaturals. Two vamps using Psych Projection can see each other. They can even battle WP to WP. Apparently, ghosts, werewolves and other entities may or may not be able to see projecting vamps, with a lean towards &quot;may&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I see your point. For me, what it would come down to is whether or not I was running a VtM game with some ghosts or a WtO with some vampires.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:22:30-07:00","id":870549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=870371#post870371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I see your point. For me, what it would come down to is whether or not I was running a VtM game with some ghosts or a WtO with some vampires.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. <br /> <br /> I've done it both ways without anything like this level of thought. Most recently it was VtM encountering wraiths and it was a nightmare for the poor vamps. I was letting them use Auspex to try to draw a bead on the wraiths attacking them, but Diff. 8 is NOT an easy target in the first place. Even when they did though, they really couldn't DO much to the wraiths. All the wraiths wanted was for them to LEAVE (they were inadvertently in the HQ for the local Emerald Legion... that's what you get for following around a Malkavian who thinks the world is a computer game...). Which they did, tails between their legs. <br /> <br /> Same setting the wraiths had a much harder time with the vamps, but the vamp in question knew EXACTLY what wraiths were and how to deal with them... Oh wait, maybe it was a Kuei Jin? I forget. It was in 2006 or 2007.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T15:33:35-07:00","id":870705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=870353#post870353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't take much a stretch to imagine why vampires can't see werewolves in the Penumbra. They're dead. They're already Shadowlands-adjacent. They are not Umbra (in the werewolf sense) adjacent. That's the realm of LIFE. That is backed up in numerous ways. Look at all of Necromancy vs.the limited nature of Spiritus. The fact that both wraiths and vampires have pale auras. Etc. Of course, the whole folderol with Psychic Projection is definitely problematic in this regard, as it really confuses exactly where the Vampire is with regard to the spirit realms of the other supernaturals. Two vamps using Psych Projection can see each other. They can even battle WP to WP. Apparently, ghosts, werewolves and other entities may or may not be able to see projecting vamps, with a lean towards &quot;may&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always gone with the assumption that the &quot;Astral Plane&quot; vampires are able to project themselves into is the Shadowlands. It seems appropriate to their themes, and doing it as one's consciousness/self-image via Auspex rather than taking one's body along for the ride as Necromancers do justifies the variance in mechanics and practitioners. The vampires' primary concern would likely be spying on the world of the living, which can be done just as handily from behind the Shroud as the Astral Umbra's Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Mage, Sorcerer, and Psychic astral projection, while mechanically similar, would be making use of the Astral Umbra and most likely encountering spirits of abstract concepts from the higher realms such travelers are actually interested in rather than wailing ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:27:24-07:00","id":874191,"title":"","content":"It basically boils down to &quot;Vampires here in the Shadowlands..... Let's go fuck them up so that they know what real death is.&quot; Or, &quot;Vampires must die!!!&quot; Especially if said vampire is a Giovanni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:53:57-07:00","id":874210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=870353#post870353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, the whole folderol with Psychic Projection is definitely problematic in this regard, as it really confuses exactly where the Vampire is with regard to the spirit realms of the other supernaturals. Two vamps using Psych Projection can see each other. They can even battle WP to WP. Apparently, ghosts, werewolves and other entities may or may not be able to see projecting vamps, with a lean towards &quot;may&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely one area that the Vampire books should have better explored. There should be more details on what the Astral Plane was like, and what kind of things happen there. We got lots of details on the Penumbra in Werewolf, and Shadowlands in Wraith, but nothing on the portion of the Umbra that vampires can travel too. Granted, not too many vampires can travel there, but there needs to be something! Some thoughts needed to be given as to what vampires could do there, and what other entities they might encounter.<br /> <br /> In my games, it is a psychic realm, a realm of thought. There are entities there - spirits of a sort - but not wraiths or Gaian spirits. And there are other voyagers, not just vampires, exploring the area. And I hold that when these different realms overlap on Earth, that there is some &quot;bleed through&quot; where they can detect one another. But it is like the concept of the Periphery in Werewolf. And sometimes projectors can cross over to another umbral realm, but this is almost always a bad thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T03:39:56-07:00","id":874383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=874210#post874210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is definitely one area that the Vampire books should have better explored. There should be more details on what the Astral Plane was like, and what kind of things happen there. We got lots of details on the Penumbra in Werewolf, and Shadowlands in Wraith, but nothing on the portion of the Umbra that vampires can travel too. Granted, not too many vampires can travel there, but there needs to be something! Some thoughts needed to be given as to what vampires could do there, and what other entities they might encounter.<br /> <br /> In my games, it is a psychic realm, a realm of thought. There are entities there - spirits of a sort - but not wraiths or Gaian spirits. And there are other voyagers, not just vampires, exploring the area. And I hold that when these different realms overlap on Earth, that there is some &amp;quot;bleed through&amp;quot; where they can detect one another. But it is like the concept of the Periphery in Werewolf. And sometimes projectors can cross over to another umbral realm, but this is almost always a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Astral Plane in VTM is supposed to be like the one in Necroscope, with the silver threads and vague location. The mapping of the various Umbrae came after VTM, and so the two don't mesh.<br /> <br /> House-ruling the Astral Plane as the Shadowlands makes the most sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:40:51-07:00","id":874616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=870705#post870705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've always gone with the assumption that the &quot;Astral Plane&quot; vampires are able to project themselves into is the Shadowlands. It seems appropriate to their themes, and doing it as one's consciousness/self-image via Auspex rather than taking one's body along for the ride as Necromancers do justifies the variance in mechanics and practitioners. The vampires' primary concern would likely be spying on the world of the living, which can be done just as handily from behind the Shroud as the Astral Umbra's Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Mage, Sorcerer, and Psychic astral projection, while mechanically similar, would be making use of the Astral Umbra and most likely encountering spirits of abstract concepts from the higher realms such travelers are actually interested in rather than wailing ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish they would just SAY that. It does make sense, but they deliberately go out of their way to create a special hybrid vamp &quot;astral form&quot; space that's not really Astral space from mage, not really the Shadowlands, not really the Penumbra, but a little bit of all three, only not. It's sort of like they are skimming along the edge of the membrane of the three Vidare from Mage, making it a &quot;place&quot; instead of mode of perception (or three). <br /> <br /> In a Vampire/Wraith crossover scene or game, I would probably just make the appropriate alteration. Astral vamps are in the Shadowlands, or maybe their immaterial and &quot;skating&quot; on the Skinlands side of the Shroud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:46:46-07:00","id":874620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=874210#post874210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is definitely one area that the Vampire books should have better explored. There should be more details on what the Astral Plane was like, and what kind of things happen there. We got lots of details on the Penumbra in Werewolf, and Shadowlands in Wraith, but nothing on the portion of the Umbra that vampires can travel too. Granted, not too many vampires can travel there, but there needs to be something! Some thoughts needed to be given as to what vampires could do there, and what other entities they might encounter.<br /> <br /> In my games, it is a psychic realm, a realm of thought. There are entities there - spirits of a sort - but not wraiths or Gaian spirits. And there are other voyagers, not just vampires, exploring the area. And I hold that when these different realms overlap on Earth, that there is some &quot;bleed through&quot; where they can detect one another. But it is like the concept of the Periphery in Werewolf. And sometimes projectors can cross over to another umbral realm, but this is almost always a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the Mage High Umbra. (But, of course, that also negates some of the text about Astral Form, where werewolves and ghosts are specfically mentioned. But it's a great House Rule to simplify matters. Having astral vamps bump into psychically projecting mystic mages, Technocrats using extra-corporeal excursion tech, perhaps some Stargazers or the like...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:30:27-07:00","id":874885,"title":"","content":"I suppose if vampire's astral forms are seen as ephemera/ectoplasm/some other ethereal option but locked on the physical side of the Gauntlet/Shroud, like that Wu Lung rote that effectively turns you into an intangible spirit, they might be perceptible to beings in all three Penumbras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T03:06:51-07:00","id":875450,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, having them intangible but in the Skinlands would be the easiest house rule, because then vamps can still spy on people but they don't usually have to worry about stepping into a world teeming with wraiths. Most cities would otherwise be full of the restless dead, so Astral Projection would be a risky business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T18:22:25-07:00","id":878296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/850777-necromancers-from-wraith-perspective?p=874383#post874383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Astral Plane in VTM is supposed to be like the one in Necroscope, with the silver threads and vague location. The mapping of the various Umbrae came after VTM, and so the two don't mesh.<br /> <br /> House-ruling the Astral Plane as the Shadowlands makes the most sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are probably right about that it is one of the inspirations, but there are many others. When First and even Second Edition Vampire came out, the Umbra as a concept either hadn't been invented or was early on. However, by Revised there really is no excuse not to include additional setting material that makes sense in the greater World of Darkness and give more more meat for people running Vampire games.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not interested in making the Astral Plane the Shadowlands, but if someone said that was the case in the game he's running, I wouldn't argue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T08:59:34-07:00","id":878771,"title":"","content":"A couple games I've played in have treated the Astral Plane as sort of between space running through the various extra-dimensional realms. Ephemeral from the outside but vast within itself. It was possible to use the Astral Plane as a jumping off point to reach places like the Umbra and the Shadowlands, though doing so was obviously very dangerous. Having your Astral form severed from your body is bad enough, having it severed on another plane of existence removed is worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T09:13:48-07:00","id":878786,"title":"","content":"That may be like the Vampire Astral Form plane, but it's not like ANYTHING in the rest of the WOD cosmology. It's more like the D&amp;D Astral Plane. Which is also like the Vampire Astral Form Plane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T12:05:01-07:00","id":878903,"title":"","content":"I personally have the idea that the Vampire Astral form allows them to travel to most areas of the umbra but they would either have to fumble around in the dark to find them or have a wraith or garou guide them to various umbral planes, due to vampires having no spiritual connection to any plane like the Garou or wraiths do.<br /> <br /> I've theory crafted every now and then, that the kindred do have their own plane but it's populated by the Beast incarnate, as spectre-like creatures who try to warp anything that passes through minds into a more vampiric state of greed,selfishness, and a slowly draining soul as the world numbs around them. It's mostly just in a concept space but if you have any ideas feel free to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}